flowchart TD
  accTitle: MISP in a digital forensics and incident response investigation
  accDescr: Evidence is collected and retained outside MISP. Selected exports enter MISP with provenance, analysts validate observations, and reviewed outputs reach hunting or response tools. Results inform further collection and reassessment.
  A[Acquire and preserve evidence] -->|Retain originals and chain of custody| B[Evidence repository]
  A -->|Export selected results| C[Import observations into MISP]
  B -.->|Case reference and integrity hash| C
  C -->|Preserve source records and time meaning| D[Validate and assess findings]
  D -->|Question about a selector| E[Approved enrichment and correlation]
  E -->|Context and alternative explanations| D
  D -->|Evidence supports a scoped action| F[Review hunt or response output]
  F -->|Deploy with scope and expiry| G[Hunting and response platforms]
  G -->|Return results and coverage| H[Reassess and document outcome]
  H -->|New evidence question| A
  class A,C,D accent;
  class B,E muted;
  class F caution;
  class G,H success;
